dsv41 patch 0064 (21.10.2026): the routed experts of 33-63-row calls as exl3_smoe row chunks, without host syncs. In
use (VLLM_EXL3_MOE_SPLIT_MAX_TOKENS=63, image v16 and later). Base: the plugin vllm_exl3_moe as in image v12
(forward.py, smoe.py).
Why: calls with more rows than the plugin's decode range (coop.rows_max = 32) and fewer than TensorFold's prompt
kernels take (64) ran on exllamav3's prefill tiers, which read the expert counts back to the host once per layer:
mixed steps under load (3 decode streams x 6 verify rows + 20-45 prompt tokens = 38-63 rows), short prompts and last
prompt chunks. In the profile of 19.10. (4 streams) a 43-row mixed step took 706 ms (CPU 699 ms, ~320 ms of it blocked
in the 40 copies; routed experts 175 ms), a 29-row prompt step on exl3_smoe 243 ms. Captured, the same sizes would take
exl3_moe's atomic tier (arrival-order sums). exl3_smoe takes at most 42 rows in one call (MAX_SLOTS = 256 picks at
top-k 6); a larger table would be a kernel change.
How: VLLM_EXL3_MOE_SPLIT_MAX_TOKENS=N: a call with coop.rows_max < m <= N rows, bf16 input and an exl3_smoe layer runs
its routed experts as exl3_smoe launches on row chunks of at most MAX_SLOTS // top_k = 42 rows, full chunks first, each
writing its rows of one bf16 output (SmoeLayer.into). Eager and under capture (static grids from m, no host read).
Calls of <= 32 rows are untouched (decode branch, moe_method.py, smoe.__call__ and the CUDA sources unchanged, so the
JIT modules keep their hash); TensorFold keeps the eager calls of >= 64 rows it serves. The shared expert keeps its
path on vLLM's aux stream; exl3_smoe has its own counters, so the chunks need no join with that stream.
Bits: exl3_smoe computes every row on its own (separate rows of the mma fragments with a whole-K fp32 chain, per-row
epilogues, a token's picks summed in pick order), so a row's output does not depend on its chunk and equals what the
row gets in a decode step; deterministic run to run. Against v12, steps with 33..N rows now round as exl3_smoe does
instead of exllamav3's tiers: T=0 texts whose prompt or last prompt chunk falls in the band can differ.
Measured (21.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v16 = v12 + 0064 together with EXL3_CPU_PIN=5-9,15-19, the plugin switch
that pins every thread of the vLLM processes to the Cortex-X925 cores; two fresh starts, decode cells against the stored
reference run of the production setup without both, kit_bench against that setup running in the same window):
kit_bench sustained (4 streams, 90 s) 118.5 -> 129.1 tok/s (+8.9 %), repeated 128.7 (+9 % against the day's reference
runs 117.8-118.5); concurrent 2 / 4 streams 73.5 / 118.3 -> 76.8 / 116.2 (concurrent 4 moved by +-4 % between two
reference runs); cost per verify round -0.62 / -0.24 % (geometric mean, two runs); T=0 texts of two runs identical to
each other and 7 of 8 identical to the reference, as expected for short prompts with 33-63 prefill rows (the JSON cell
at T=0 wrote another text: tokens per round -16.7 % at -2.6 % ms per round, which takes the tok/s geometric mean to
-2.6 / -3.1 %); corruption test (30K/100K, 2 each) 0 hits; lowest free memory under load 2,300 MiB head / 3,515 MiB
worker. The shares of 0064 and of the pin were not measured separately.
Switch: VLLM_EXL3_MOE_SPLIT_MAX_TOKENS=63 (0 / unset = off = v12; values >= 64 also take captured calls of >= 64 rows,
never TensorFold's eager ones).

